---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import InfoPage from "@components/InfoPage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Community Guidelines | NepalRanks"
  description="NepalRanks community guidelines: argue with evidence, no harassment, no brand wars, honest reviews, respect moderators and the path to appeals."
>
  <InfoPage eyebrow="Community">
    <h1>Community guidelines</h1>
    <p>
      A ranking is only as trustworthy as the discussion around it. These
      guidelines apply to comments, votes and every public corner of NepalRanks.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Rate the experience, not the person</h2>
    <p>
      Talk about service, quality, price and reliability. Attacks on individuals,
      employees, communities, castes, regions or businesses' owners are removed.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Evidence beats volume</h2>
    <p>
      "Two failed transactions in a week, branch at Baneshwor" persuades. Ten
      accounts copy-pasting one slogan is a brand war, and brand wars get the whole
      discussion thread locked, not just the losers.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No paid promotion, no fake reviews</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not post scripted praise for payment, exposure or fun.</li>
      <li>Do not impersonate a business account; official responses are labelled and verified.</li>
      <li>Vote manipulation across accounts is treated as platform abuse, not speech.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Keep it Nepali-sane</h2>
    <p>
      Disagreement is the whole point; harassment is not. No slurs, no doxxing, no
      screenshots of private messages, no pile-ons. Languages used in comments:
      English and Nepali both welcome, write the way you speak.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Moderation and appeals</h2>
    <p>
      Moderators (who cannot change rankings) may hide comments and freeze voting
      rights. Removals are logged in the moderation queue and appealable through the
      <a href="contact/">contact page</a>. Sanctions escalate: hide → vote freeze → ban
      (once accounts exist).
    </p>

    <h2>6. How enforcement works today</h2>
    <p>
      Live comments appear immediately and are reviewed in the daily moderation run, anything
      breaking these rules is hidden then, and repeat abuse loses voting rights. Vote limits are
      enforced technically. Formal reports and appeals open with the contact mail channel;
      account-level bans (email-backed) arrive with Gmail sign-in.
    </p>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
